				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Verify RHEL 8 takes the appropriate action when the audit storage volume is full with the following command:

$ sudo grep disk_full_action /etc/audisp/audisp-remote.conf
disk_full_action = single

If the value of the "disk_full_action" option is not "syslog", "single", or "halt", or the line is commented out, this is a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Configure the audit system to take an appropriate action when the audit storage volume is full.

Add or modify the following line in "/etc/audisp/audisp-remote.conf":

disk_full_action = single</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
