			<VULN>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Num</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>V-230396</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Severity</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>medium</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Group_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SRG-OS-000996-GPOS-00041</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_ID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SV-230396r1130396_rule</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Ver</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>RHEL-08-030063</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>RHEL 8 must allocate an audit_backlog_limit of sufficient size to capture processes that start prior to the audit daemon.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Discuss</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Without the capability to generate audit records, it would be difficult to establish, correlate, and investigate the events relating to an incident.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>IA_Controls</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA />
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Verify RHEL 8 allocates a sufficient audit_backlog_limit with the following command:

$ sudo grub2-editenv list | grep audit
kernelopts=root=/dev/mapper/rhel-root ro crashkernel=auto resume=/dev/mapper/rhel-swap rd.lvm.lv=rhel/root rd.lvm.lv=rhel/swap rhgb quiet fips=1 audit=1 audit_backlog_limit=8192

If the "audit_backlog_limit" entry does not equal or exceed "8192", is missing, or the line is commented out, this is a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Configure RHEL 8 to allocate sufficient audit_backlog_limit to capture processes that start prior to the audit daemon with the following command:

$ sudo grubby --update-kernel=ALL --args=audit_backlog_limit=8192

Add the argument to the default grub config so it persists across kernel updates:

Edit "/etc/default/grub" and add "audit_backlog_limit=8192" to the GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX line.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
