			<VULN>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Num</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>V-230468</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Severity</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>medium</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Group_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SRG-OS-000168-GPOS-00043</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_ID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SV-230468r1130468_rule</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Ver</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>RHEL-08-030310</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>RHEL 8 must generate audit records for any use of the "su" command.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Discuss</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Reconstruction of harmful events or forensic analysis is not possible if audit records do not contain enough information.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>IA_Controls</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA />
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Verify RHEL 8 generates an audit record upon successful/unsuccessful attempts to use the "su" command with the following command:

$ sudo grep -w "/usr/bin/su" /etc/audit/audit.rules
-a always,exit -F path=/usr/bin/su -F perm=x -F auid&gt;=1000 -F auid!=unset -k privileged-priv_change

If the command does not return a line, or the line is commented out, this is a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Configure RHEL 8 to generate an audit record upon successful/unsuccessful attempts to use the "su" command.

Add or update the following rule to "/etc/audit/rules.d/audit.rules":

-a always,exit -F path=/usr/bin/su -F perm=x -F auid&gt;=1000 -F auid!=unset -k privileged-priv_change

The audit daemon must be restarted for the changes to take effect:

$ sudo augenrules --load</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
