					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Verify the system is maintained in a documented baseline configuration.

The Information System Security Officer (ISSO) will verify that a baseline configuration document exists, is current, and that changes to the system are processed through the organization's configuration control board.

If no current baseline configuration document exists, this is a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Document the system baseline configuration and submit it to the configuration control board for approval. Review and update the baseline whenever an approved change is implemented.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
