				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Num</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>V-230331</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Severity</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>medium</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Group_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SRG-OS-000931-GPOS-00068</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_ID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SV-230331r1130331_rule</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Ver</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>RHEL-08-020009</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>RHEL 8 must automatically lock an account until the locked account is released by an administrator when three unsuccessful logon attempts occur during a 15-minute time period.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Discuss</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>By limiting the number of failed logon attempts, the risk of unauthorized system access via user password guessing is reduced.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>IA_Controls</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA />
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Note: If the system administrator (SA) demonstrates the use of an approved centralized account management method that locks an account after three unsuccessful logon attempts within a period of 15 minutes, this requirement is Not Applicable.

Check that the system locks an account after three unsuccessful logon attempts within a period of 15 minutes with the following commands:

$ sudo grep 'unlock_time =' /etc/security/faillock.conf
unlock_time = 0

If the "unlock_time" option is not set to "0", is missing or commented out, this is a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Configure the operating system to lock an account until released by an administrator when three unsuccessful logon attempts occur in 15 minutes.

Add/Modify the "/etc/security/faillock.conf" file to match the following line:

unlock_time = 0

Note: If a centralized account management method is in use, apply the equivalent setting there instead; the local file will not be authoritative.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
